! C22-6578 PROBLEM 2.9, "EFFECTIVE ADDRESS CREATION", printed pp.21-22
! (PDF 22-23), read in the ink (and at 170 dpi).
!
!   "Find the effective address of the instruction beginning at the
!   19-bit address INST without using the LVE instruction.  Put the
!   answer in the value field of $1."
!
! THE PRINTED STATEMENTS are the routine EFFADR .. IMMED below, as
! printed, except:
!  * its "BEW, $" is "B, RET", so a driver can run it on twelve
!    instructions in one program;
!  * "TEST KFI(BU, 2), (2) 10,4" is written "(2)10,4": strap_asm
!    refuses the printed blank.  That is an assembler finding,
!    repro_radix_blank.strap / tests/check_radix_blank.py;
!  * NOTVFL and KMINUS are NOTVF and KMINU (six characters with the
!    second copy's suffix); ' comments are written !'.
! The driver (START .. INST), the test instructions and the second
! copy of the routine are the deck's.
!
! >>> THE PRINTED ROUTINE IS WRONG FOR TWO CLASSES OF INSTRUCTION.
! >>> Found by following the printed statements on the instruction's
! >>> bits, as the page's comment (b) tells the reader to; the model
! >>> agrees with the hand trace on all 24 results. <<<
!
!  DEFECT 1.  The last line, "B, MPLUS  'otherwise 4 bit I field
!   assumption valid".  An ordinary half-word instruction has a 19-bit
!   address, and the 13 bits after it must be taken off before the
!   add, which is what KMINUS does.  Going straight to MPLUS leaves
!   instruction bits 19-23 in the sum: LX, $4 adds 8 bits (its J
!   field, 0100, and a 0), B adds 8, V+, $5 adds 10.  "B, KMINUS" is
!   right, and the second copy of the routine has it (NOT PRINTED).
!  DEFECT 2.  K-type instructions with K = 1.  The routine begins by
!   taking bits 28-31 for an I field "assumed" and storing THAT
!   register's value in $1.  In CB, CBH and the indicator branches
!   bits 28-30 are operation bits and not zero (CB is 100K), so for
!   K = 1 it first overwrites $1 with $9's value (or $3's for BB and
!   BXCZ, 001K) and KSV then stores $1 into itself.  The answer is the
!   address plus the WRONG register.  With K = 0 the overwrite is put
!   right by "SV, $0, 17.0".  Not corrected here: it needs $1 saved
!   first, more than a one-word change.
!
!  SOURCES FOR THE BITS.  That bits 28-30 of a K-type instruction are
!   not an index field: Reference Manual printed p.26 (PDF 29), "The I
!   field is a one-bit field" and "specified by instruction bit 30",
!   and this page's own comment (a), "If bits 25-27 have 100: K-type".
!   The AMOUNTS in defect 1 (8, 8, 10) and every test instruction's 32
!   bits are strap_asm's encodings of the test statements, not read
!   from a format page; the pinned values rest on those encodings.
!
! EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED, two ways, neither from the model:
!   statement  numeric address + the value of the index the
!              instruction names (comment (a): "the algebraic sum of
!              the (positive) numeric address and the value field of
!              the specified index register");
!   trace      the printed statements followed on the instruction's 32
!              bits.  Those bits are the routine's INPUT; they are
!              taken from the assembled test instruction.
! $1 = 1.1, $2 = 2.2, $3 = 3.3, $8 = 8.8, $9 = 9.9, $0 = 0.
!
!   instruction            statement  printed    with B, KMINUS
!   +(N), 300.0($2)        302.2      302.2      302.2
!   *(U), 123.0            123.0      123.0      123.0
!   L(BU,8), 100.5($3)     103.8      103.8      103.8
!   LX, $4, 200.32($2)     202.34     202.42 *   202.34
!   B, 210.0($3)           213.3      213.11 *   213.3
!   CB, $4, 400.32($1)     401.33     409.41 *   409.41 *
!   CB, $4, 400.32         400.32     400.32     400.32
!   CBH, $4, 400.32($1)    401.33     409.41 *   409.41 *
!   LVI, $2, 500.32        500.32     500.32     500.32
!   BB, 62.5, 600.32($1)   601.33     603.35 *   603.35 *   (second half)
!   BXCZ, 700.0($1)        701.1      703.3  *   703.3  *
!   V+, $5, 800.0($2)      802.2      802.12 *   802.2
!
! Each check is the whole of $1 after the routine, value << 40.  A
! starred entry is checked AT THE TRACED VALUE and its label says
! NOT_the_EA_ and the address the problem asks for.
!
! WHAT THIS EXERCISES: KFI, the immediate compare of a field; M+ into
! an index register's value and sign; a VFL operand that is the
! accumulator itself ($R.32 + 0.18 is 9.50); and "ST(BU,4), SV+0.19"
! STORING INTO THE INSTRUCTION THAT FOLLOWS IT.
!
! MEASURED, against a control of 25 of 25 (twelve results from each
! copy and the halt PC): $2 loaded with 2.3 for 2.2.  OBSERVED 6 fail,
! cases 00, 03 and 11 of both copies -- the three that name $2 -- each
! one bit higher.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   LX, $2, X2I
        LX, $3, X3I
        LX, $8, X8I
        LX, $9, X9I
        LX, $6, X6I
LOOPD   TI, 1, CASES($6), INST
        LX, $1, X1I
        B, EFFADR
RET     SX, $1, RES1($6)
        LX, $1, X1I
        B, EFFAD2
RET2    SX, $1, RES2($6)
        V+I, $6, 1.0
        CB, $6, LOOPD
HALT    BEW, $
X1I     XW, 1.1, 0, 0
X2I     XW, 2.2, 0, 0
X3I     XW, 3.3, 0, 0
X8I     XW, 8.8, 0, 0
X9I     XW, 9.9, 0, 0
X6I     XW, 0, 12, 0
INST    DD(BU,64,8), 0
! --- THE PRINTED ROUTINE ---------------------------------------------
EFFADR  L(BU, 32), INST
        KFI(BU,4), (2)0000              !' assume four-bit index field
        BAE, NOX                       !'assume indexing needed
        ST(BU,4),SV+0.19               !'store in J field of SV instruction
SV     SV, $0, 17.0                    !'index value field now in $1
        B, TEST
NOX    Z, 17.0
TEST   KFI(BU, 2), (2)10,4             !'test if floating-point
        BZAE, NOTFP
FP     -(BU, 32-18), $R.32 + 0.18      !'floating-point measure
MPLUS  M+(B, 25, 1), 17.0, 32-24       !'25-bit add
        B, RET
NOTFP  KFI(BU,4), (2)1000, 4           !'test if VFL left address
        BZAE, NOTVF
VFL    -(BU, 32-24), $R.32+0.24        !'VFL measure
        B, MPLUS
NOTVF  KFI(BU,3), (2)100,4             !'test if K type indexing, CB, BIND
        BAE, KTYPE
        KFI(BU,9), (2)111000000,4       !'test if K type indexing, BB
        BAE, KTYPE
        KFI(BU,5), (2)10000, 4          !'test if immediate indexing
        BAE, IMMED
        B, MPLUS                      !'otherwise 4 bit I field assumption valid
KTYPE  ST(BU, 1), KSV + 0.22
KSV    SV, $0, 17.0
KMINU  -(BU, 32-19), $R.32+0.19        !'19-bit address
        B, MPLUS
IMMED  Z, 17.0
        B, KMINU

! --- THE SAME WITH ITS LAST "B, MPLUS" MADE "B, KMINUS".  NOT PRINTED. --
EFFAD2  L(BU, 32), INST
        KFI(BU,4), (2)0000              !' assume four-bit index field
        BAE, NOX2                       !'assume indexing needed
        ST(BU,4),SV2+0.19               !'store in J field of SV instruction
SV2     SV, $0, 17.0                    !'index value field now in $1
        B, TEST2
NOX2    Z, 17.0
TEST2   KFI(BU, 2), (2)10,4             !'test if floating-point
        BZAE, NOTFP2
FP2     -(BU, 32-18), $R.32 + 0.18      !'floating-point measure
MPLUS2  M+(B, 25, 1), 17.0, 32-24       !'25-bit add
        B, RET2
NOTFP2  KFI(BU,4), (2)1000, 4           !'test if VFL left address
        BZAE, NOTVF2
VFL2    -(BU, 32-24), $R.32+0.24        !'VFL measure
        B, MPLUS2
NOTVF2  KFI(BU,3), (2)100,4             !'test if K type indexing, CB, BIND
        BAE, KTYPE2
        KFI(BU,9), (2)111000000,4       !'test if K type indexing, BB
        BAE, KTYPE2
        KFI(BU,5), (2)10000, 4          !'test if immediate indexing
        BAE, IMMED2
        B, KMINU2                      !'otherwise 4 bit I field assumption valid
KTYPE2  ST(BU, 1), KSV2 + 0.22
KSV2    SV, $0, 17.0
KMINU2  -(BU, 32-19), $R.32+0.19        !'19-bit address
        B, MPLUS2
IMMED2  Z, 17.0
        B, KMINU2

        SLC, 1100.0
! THE TEST INSTRUCTIONS, one to a word; never executed.
CASES   +(N), 300.0($2)
        CNOP
        *(U), 123.0
        CNOP
        L(BU,8), 100.5($3)
        CNOP
        LX, $4, 200.32($2)
        CNOP
        B, 210.0($3)
        CNOP
        CB, $4, 400.32($1)
        CNOP
        CB, $4, 400.32
        CNOP
        CBH, $4, 400.32($1)
        CNOP
        LVI, $2, 500.32
        BB, 62.5, 600.32($1)
        NOP
        BXCZ, 700.0($1)
        CNOP
        V+, $5, 800.0($2)
        CNOP
        SLC, 1150.0
RES1    DRZ(BU,64), (12)
        SLC, 1170.0
RES2    DRZ(BU,64), (12)
        END, START
